  booktitle={2026 4th International Conference on Intelligent Data Communication Technologies and Internet of Things (IDCIoT)}, 
  title={Compact Wideband Slotted Swastika Shaped Electromagnetic Bandgap Structures for mm-Wave Communication}, 
  year={2026},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={227-230},
  abstract={This paper introduces a small wideband Swastikatype Electromagnetic Bandgap (EBG) structure for mm-wave communication platforms. The suggested EBG unit cell is built on a $3.6 \times 3.6 ~\text{mm}^{2}$ square FR-4 substrate that is 0.8 mm thick. To obtain better bandgap properties and harmonic suppression in the mm-wave band, a metallic patch in the shape of a swastika is merged with several circular slots. A broad operational band spanning 29.5 to 33.6 GHz, or a bandwidth of 4.1 GHz around the central frequency of 32 GHz, is demonstrated using full-wave models. The suggested EBG unit cell is ideal for incorporation in compact $5 \mathrm{G} / 6 \mathrm{G}$ front-end modules and dense mm-wave antenna arrays owing to its small size and broad stopband capabilities.},
